# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: dcl-tui-completion — complete the integrated DCL text-UI renderer for headless / "-" commands
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: feature-dcl-tui

* Context

clautolisp has a *pluggable* DCL renderer (=autolisp-dcl/source/runtime.lisp=,
=dcl-renderer= struct: open/run/close/set-tile/mode/image-paint/populate-list
fns). Two renderers ship: a Qt GUI via a sexp subprocess protocol
(=subprocess-renderer.lisp=, partial — tracked separately in the opendcl
epic) and a pure-CL **terminal (TUI) renderer** (=terminal.lisp=), installed
as the default at load (=eval-when= at end of terminal.lisp). So headless
runs already drive dialogs through the TUI.

Reference (AutoCAD/BricsCAD): prefixing a command with =-= runs its
*command-line* form instead of the dialog. For custom DCL there is no
vendor-provided =-= fallback — the developer writes one. clautolisp's TUI
renderer is effectively that command-line form for ANY dialog, applied
automatically when no GUI is present. This issue completes it so =-=-style /
headless invocations that call up DCL work end-to-end.

* Progress (clautolisp 1.7.15) — greet works headless

Three real bugs fixed; the =greet= example now runs fully over the TUI
(=name=Claude= + =accept= → "Hello, Claude!"; =cancel= → "Cancelled."):

- =terminal-handle-line= short-circuited =accept=/=ok=/=cancel=/=quit= to a
  status BEFORE looking up the tile, so an accept button's registered action
  (which reads tiles via get_tile and calls done_dialog) never fired. Now a
  named tile is handled by firing its action first.
- The DCL reserved variables were interned as =$KEY$= / =$VALUE$= / =$REASON$=
  (trailing =$=); AutoLISP DCL — and pjb's own greet.lsp — use =$key= / =$value=
  / =$reason= / =$data= (no trailing =$=; the reader upcases =$value= → =$VALUE=).
  Mismatch → =$value= read nil. Fixed the names; =$reason= is now the integer
  reason code (1 select / 2 changed / 3 focus-lost / 4 double-click) via
  =dcl-reason-code=. Corrected the =runtime-action-callback-binding-symbols=
  test (it had codified the buggy spelling) and added the integration test
  =dcl-terminal-renderer-drives-dialog-headless= (builtins-core, stdin-driven).
- =ok_cancel= is NOT expanded into accept/cancel button tiles (it renders as a
  =<ok-cancel>= placeholder), so its accept/cancel were unreachable from the
  tile walk. =terminal-fire-registered= fires the action registered under
  =accept=/=cancel= even without an explicit tile.

* Progress (clautolisp 1.7.18) — TUI complete; only the Qt GUI app remains

Items 1-5 DONE on branch =feature-dcl-tui=; the TUI renderer is complete and
every acceptance criterion except the Qt C++ app (item 6) is met.

- **Item 1 — clusters expand at load.** =expand-predefined-tile= matched the
  parser's =:OK-CANCEL= keyword against the underscore registry keys
  (=ok_cancel=) and silently never fired. Fixed the normalisation
  (downcase + dashes→underscores) and made it recurse; added =errtile=,
  =ok_cancel_err=, =ok_cancel_help_errtile=. ok_only / ok_cancel /
  ok_cancel_help now become real =accept= / =cancel= / =help= =:button= and
  =errtile= =:text= tiles that both renderers walk. The =<ok-cancel>=
  placeholder is gone; =terminal-fire-registered= kept as a harmless fallback.
- **Item 2 — interactive tile types.** toggle (key=1 sets / bare key flips —
  the greet =shout= toggle round-trips), radio_button / radio_column (mutually
  exclusive; the cluster key returns the selected button key), popup_list /
  list_box (select by index or name; stores the index), slider (clamped to
  min/max), image / image_button. Each renders legibly and round-trips through
  get_tile.
- **Item 3 — renderer selection.** =--dcl tui|gui|auto= (shared CLI spec +
  =parse-dcl-mode= + a =cli-options= slot). auto = GUI only when a driver is
  configured AND stdout is a TTY, else TUI (so headless/piped = TUI); tui =
  force the command-line form (clautolisp's spelling of AutoCAD's =-command=);
  gui = subprocess driver, warn+fallback to TUI when none configured. Wired in
  main.lisp (=select-and-install-dcl-renderer=, using =output-stream-is-tty-p=)
  and documented in the user manual ("DCL dialogs — renderer selection").
- **Item 4 — $reason breadth.** The TUI input grammar carries a modifier:
  =KEY= (selected, 1), =KEY=VALUE= (changed, 2, for edit_box/slider; a select
  for list/popup/toggle/radio), =KEY==VALUE= (double-click, 4), =KEY!= (lost
  focus, 3). All four codes reachable and tested.
- **Item 5 — listpick headless.** =examples/listpick/listpick.lsp= now loads
  its .dcl by a relative name (was a hard-coded /Users/pjb path) and runs
  headless; a list_box picker integration test added.

Validation deliverable: =examples/all-widgets/= (all-widgets.dcl +
all-widgets.lsp + README.org) — one of every standard DCL tile, a labelled
value report for cross-CAD diffing, runs fully in TUI mode headless.

Tests: pure-renderer FiveAM tests per tile type + cluster expansion + the four
reason codes (autolisp-dcl/tests); two stdin-driven integration tests over the
full get_tile/action stack in a =;;;; DCL widgets= block (builtins-core). Whole
suite green (Fail: 0).

Remaining: **item 6** — the Qt C++ GUI app (=tools/clautolisp-gui-qt=). The
Lisp-side subprocess renderer is complete (announces the tile tree via
=tile->sexp=, forwards set_tile/mode/focus/populate_list/image_paint, consumes
=:action= / =:done=); what is unbuilt/unexercised here is the C++ side —
rendering each widget and emitting =:action= / =:done= events back. Tracked by
the opendcl epic (=opendcl-renderer-scaffold=, =opendcl-controls=,
=opendcl-wire-protocol=). Kept OPEN until that lands.

* Remaining work

1. **Expand predefined clusters at load** (ok_cancel, ok_only, ok_cancel_help,
   ok_cancel_help_errtile, ...) into their constituent =:button= tiles, so
   accept/cancel/help are real tiles both renderers see. This is the proper
   fix (the =terminal-fire-registered= stopgap only covers accept/cancel by
   name); it also benefits the Qt renderer. Currently they are single
   unexpanded tile types rendered as =<ok-cancel>= placeholders.
2. **Unhandled / incomplete tile types in the terminal renderer**: =:toggle=
   and cluster tiles render as =<toggle>= / =<ok-cancel>= placeholders rather
   than proper widgets, and the toggle value does not round-trip (=shout=1= in
   greet did not reach =(= $shout "1")=). Cover toggle, radio_button /
   radio_column, popup_list, slider, image / image_button interaction + value
   storage, matching what get_tile expects.
3. **Renderer selection / the "-" semantics**: define how TUI vs GUI is
   chosen — auto (non-TTY or no GUI backend → TUI), an explicit CLI flag, and
   the =-=-command convention (force the command-line/TUI form even when a GUI
   is available). Today the terminal renderer is the hardcoded default and the
   Qt renderer installs itself when the GUI runs.
4. **$reason breadth**: only =:reason-selected= is emitted by the renderers;
   wire :reason-changed (edit-in-progress), :reason-lost-focus, and
   :reason-double-click where the interaction model supports them.
5. **Second example**: make =examples/listpick= (a list_box picker) work
   headless too, as a second acceptance fixture.
6. Complete the Qt GUI DCL renderer (partial) — its own opendcl-epic issues.

* Acceptance criteria

- =greet= and =listpick= examples run fully over the TUI headless (all their
  tiles interactive, values round-trip through get_tile).
- Predefined clusters are expanded into real tiles; =<...>= placeholders gone.
- Renderer selection (auto headless + explicit force) is documented in the
  clautolisp user manual, incl. how a =-= invocation gets the TUI.
- FiveAM tests cover each interactive tile type over the terminal renderer.
